-- title:
--   Original ruin-stopped source HJB supersolution and one-sided Ito bound imply full discounted dividends under measurable localisation
-- statement:
--   For the actual original spectrally negative Levy path, admissible dividends, finite capped stopped clock and original ruin, positive discount and source HJB generator and derivative inequalities, and corrected boundary w(0)>=0, one-sided Ito-Meyer domination with a centred integrable martingale and nonpositive integrable drift implies the expected terminal-plus-complete-Stieltjes cash bound. Only a.e. strong measurability, not independent integrability, of the original terminal and cash observables is assumed; both integrabilities are proved from the one-sided budget via Proved 30b2e334, then Proved 06a07e43 delivers the exact real and ENNReal expected dividend bound. BV C1 and UBV C2 branches remain distinct. The one-sided Ito domination and source martingale/drift facts remain explicit open stochastic premises.
-- source:
--   Avram Prop 4(i) Eq (5.11)-(5.13); composition of two already Proved source-faithful conditional bridge theorems 30b2e334 and 06a07e43.

